Resolve the repository root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` and run all commands from there.

Deploy the exact verified commit immediately after it is pushed; the pull request does not need to be merged. From the pushed local branch, run `npm run prod:deploy:pushed`.

The pushed-release command must confirm that local `HEAD` exactly matches `origin/<current-branch>`, create an isolated clean release worktree at that remote commit, and delegate to `npm run prod:deploy`. The deploy command owns the immutable image build, SQLite/uploads backup, health-checked Compose replacement, release manifest, and automatic rollback. Do not run a Docker reset, copy a live database, or run a separate snapshot command.

Never print, archive, or commit production paths, environment files, credentials, tailnet identifiers, database contents, uploads, or other private machine data.
